# Nightly MySQL dumps (docker-compose mounts ./backups into db-backup).
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this every dump — i.e. every user's
# encrypted exchange API keys, emails and trades — gets baked into the app
# image and ships anywhere the image goes. Keep dumps out of the build context.
/backups/
*.sql
*.sql.gz

coverage
dist
build

# helpful for keeping context tight
README.md
docs

# Uploaded chart screenshots — same reason as /backups: never bake user
# files into the image.
/uploads/
